            "html": "<p>The difficulty is not that the players lack skill in arithmetic. They can add six and one as readily as they can add one and one. Their problem is that ordinary arithmetic describes <strong>what has happened</strong>, while their agreement concerns <strong>what has not yet happened</strong>. No one knows the next throw. Yet money must be committed now. Is there a reasonable way to compare two uncertain possibilities before either occurs?</p>"
