            "html": "<p>What changed? We stopped counting <strong>names of totals</strong> and started counting <strong>elementary outcomes</strong>: the specific possible results of the two dice. Their complete collection is called the <strong>sample space</strong>, conventionally written Ω in modern notation. An <strong>event</strong> is a set of outcomes satisfying some condition; “the total is 7” is an event containing six pairs: <bdi dir=\"ltr\">(1,6)</bdi>, <bdi dir=\"ltr\">(2,5)</bdi>, <bdi dir=\"ltr\">(3,4)</bdi>, <bdi dir=\"ltr\">(4,3)</bdi>, <bdi dir=\"ltr\">(5,2)</bdi>, and <bdi dir=\"ltr\">(6,1)</bdi>. None of this modern notation should be attributed literally to Cardano. It is the present-day language with which we reconstruct the insight.</p>"
