            "html": "<p>The assumption that the dice are fair and independent is essential. Each face of the first die has probability <bdi dir=\"ltr\">1/6</bdi>; each face of the second does too; and the result of one does not affect the result of the other. Consequently each ordered pair has probability <strong><bdi dir=\"ltr\">1/36</bdi></strong>. If one die were weighted, listing 36 combinations would still be possible, but counting them as equally likely would no longer be justified.</p>"
