            "html": "<p>Now the wager has a defensible numerical answer. Six equally likely pairs produce a 7, while just one produces a 2. Thus the chance of 7 is <strong><bdi dir=\"ltr\">6/36 = 1/6 ≈ 16.7%</bdi></strong> and the chance of 2 is <strong><bdi dir=\"ltr\">1/36 ≈ 2.8%</bdi></strong>. The player wagering on 7 has six times as many winning elementary outcomes. Equal prizes for the two outcomes would not balance their chances.</p>"
